<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Chahamanas of Jalor</h1><p class="st-meta">1160 CE – 1311 CE (approx.) · capital Jalor</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Chauhan Rajput dynasty of Jalor in Marwar, famous for its last stand against the armies of Alauddin Khalji.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalore">Jalor</a> branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chahamanas</a> (Chauhans) descended from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chahamanas-of-naddula">Chahamanas of Naddula</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kirtipala">Kirtipala</a>, a son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nadol">Naddula</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alhana">Alhana</a>, captured the hill fort of Jalor from the Paramaras around 1160 and founded a separate line, known as the Songara Chauhans after the fort's Sonagiri hill.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kings held a strong fort controlling routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and the Indo-Gangetic plain, and acted at times as allies or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaulukya-dynasty">Chaulukyas of Gujarat</a> and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udayasimha-of-jalor">Udayasimha</a> extended the kingdom and repelled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iltutmish">Iltutmish</a>. Jain temples and inscriptions at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalore">Jalor</a> record the patronage of merchants and rulers alike.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanhadadeva">Kanhadadeva</a> resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin Khalji</a>, who took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siwana">Siwana</a> and then besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalore">Jalor</a>, capturing it in 1311; the king and his son Viramadeva were killed. The story became the subject of the 15th-century epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanhadade-prabandha">Kanhadade Prabandha</a>. Jalor passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1160 CE – 1311 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.79%;width:3.00%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1160 CE – 1311 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jalor</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kirtipala, Udayasimha, Kanhadadeva</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Jainism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit, Old Rajasthani</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Songara Chauhans, Kingdom of Jalore</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1236&amp;focus=chahamanas-of-jalor" aria-label="Chahamanas of Jalor on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6810 1325 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chahamanas of Jalor lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7018 1385h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7130 1581h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7130 1581h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=1236&amp;focus=chahamanas-of-jalor">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
